    | §C9.a NOVELTY_CHALLENGES — Divisor-only restriction at primorial Q: does `M_W^{div}(n) := Σ_{q | W, q sqf} mu(gcd(q,n)) / phi(q/gcd(q,n))` admit an exact pointwise closed form? (cross-domain: NONE; project-internal Möbius collapse + Hölder-reduced Ramanujan sum) | BUILT | E | S208 novelty-mode session refining E2.1 / S191 / C9. **Theorem (S208, proven analytically; verified pointwise to machine epsilon at N ≤ 10⁶ across 10 conductors).** For every squarefree integer W ≥ 1 and every positive integer n, `M_W^{div}(n) = [gcd(n, W) = 1] · W / phi(W)`. For non-squarefree W, the identity holds with W replaced by rad(W). **Proof**: factorise the squarefree-divisor lattice of W by intersection with `{p|W : p|n}`; the alternating-sum collapse `Σ_{A⊆P_n}(-1)^|A| = [P_n = ∅]` factors out, leaving `∏_{p|W} p/(p-1) = W/φ(W)` on the coprime branch. **Empirical verification**: 10 conductors `W ∈ {2, 6, 30, 210, 2310 (primorials); 15, 105 (squarefree non-primorial); 12, 60, 420 (non-squarefree, rad ∈ {6, 30, 210})}` × `N ∈ {10⁵, 10⁶}`. F1/F2/F3 (pointwise identity at squarefree primorial / squarefree non-primorial / radical-reduced non-squarefree): max abs_err 8.88·10⁻¹⁶ (machine epsilon). F4 (mean = 1): all in [0.999997, 1.000000]. F5 (L² closed form `||T_W^{div} − chi_P||²/N` matches explicit prime-distribution count `(n_coprime_primes (T_val−1)² + n_coprime_comp T_val² + n_W) / N` with `T_val = (π(N)/N) · W/φ(W)`): rel_err < 10⁻⁹ on every cell. F6 (Pearson_full > Pearson_div for W ∈ {6, 30, 210, 2310}): PASS, gap = 0.028, 0.089, 0.177, 0.281 respectively at N=10⁵; gap = 0 at W=2 because the only squarefree integers ≤ 2 are exactly the divisors of 2. **Algorithmic consequence**: T_W^{div}(n) is informationally equivalent to a wheel-rad(W) sieve scaled by π(N)/N · rad(W)/φ(rad(W)); the divisor-only restriction inherits all sieve barriers (no polylog opening). The Pearson gap to full T_W locates the prime-discriminating signal in the **non-divisor squarefree conductors** q ≤ W (q squarefree but q ∤ W), capturing 31% of the full Pearson at W=2310. **What's new beyond S191 (C9)**: S191 stated only the corollary at coprime n (`T_W | gcd=1 = (π/N)·W/φ(W)`); S208 proves the identity **on the full domain** (zero at non-coprime n) for all squarefree W, with explicit radical reduction for non-squarefree W. **Refines E2.1**: the wheel-density factor φ(W)/W is now the value of an explicit pointwise scalar field, not merely an asymptotic rank quotient. **Cross-domain ingredient**: NONE; project-internal one-line Möbius collapse. **Falsifier**: any (W, n) with `M_W^{div}(n) ≠ [gcd(n, rad(W)) = 1] · rad(W)/φ(rad(W))` by more than 10⁻¹², OR mean ⟨M_W^{div}⟩_n ≠ 1 ± O(1/N), OR Pearson(chi_P, T_W) ≤ Pearson(chi_P, T_W^{div}) at any W ≥ 6, OR L² closed form deviates by more than rel_err 10⁻⁹. None observed across 10 W × 2 N cells. **Successors proposed (S208)**: C9.a.i (off-divisor squarefree expansion: decompose 0.281 Pearson gap at W=2310 by conductor q; predicted Selberg-Delange `~1/φ(p)²` per prime contribution, 1 session); C9.a.ii (Lean formalisation of the divisor-only identity via L6 Hölder reduction + Möbius collapse, ~50-line Lean target, 1 session); C9.a.iii (Λ-modulated divisor-only sum `μ²(q)λ(q)c_q(n)/φ(q)` — does the parity-twisted weight also yield a closed-form scalar on the residue lattice mod W?, 1 session). See `experiments/constructions/spike_divisor_only_wheel/`, `archive/sessions/session208_c9a_divisor_only_wheel.md`. | 208 |
    
